Third-party notice

This plugin reads data that other, separately-licensed software exports. It
does not bundle, modify, or redistribute any part of that software.

- AIDA64 (FinalWire Ltd.) — proprietary commercial software. This plugin
  reads the sensor values AIDA64 exports to the Windows registry
  (`HKCU\Software\FinalWire\AIDA64\SensorValues`) or to the
  `AIDA64_SensorValues` shared-memory mapping. See
  docs/aida64-sensor-export.md for the observed format.
- HWiNFO (HWiNFO Community / Martin Malik) — proprietary software. This
  plugin reads the `HKLM|HKCU\Software\HWiNFO64\VSB` registry values and the
  `Global\HWiNFO_SENS_SM2` shared-memory section. See
  docs/hwinfo-sensor-format.md.

IMPORTANT — HWiNFO shared-memory specification

The official HWiNFO shared-memory layout is **not public**. Its author states
on the official forum (pinned thread "Shared Memory Support") that the
specification is provided by e-mail only, under conditions that include:
consumers of the interface must be freeware without advertising, and
open-source applications must keep the interfacing part in binary (closed)
form.

The layout implemented in `lib/hwinfo.js` was derived independently, by
observing the bytes of a running instance and cross-checking with public
third-party reverse-engineering and open-source parsers. It is published here
as documentation of what was observed, not as a licensed or authorized
specification.

If you intend to distribute this plugin publicly, review that condition
against your own distribution. If you are the rights holder and want this
removed or changed, open an issue and it will be handled promptly.
